IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc32-nif-1`

-- ccc32-tests-nif-1.l4 -- tests for ccc32-nif-1.l4 (amendments not in force: 2018 c. 16 s. 190, 2021 c. 2 s. 1(2.1), 2023 c. 28 s. 35, 2024 c. 33 s. 2).
-- Every expected value is decided by reading the provision, and written beside the assertion. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `2018 c. 16 s. 190 and subsection 737(1)`

-- 190: if Bill C-28 receives royal assent, subsection 737(1) is replaced on the first day on which both provisions are in force.
#ASSERT `2018 c 16 s 190 subsection 737(1) is replaced by the following` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2018 c 16 s 190 subsection 737(1) is replaced by the following` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the "If" fails: the text's no within the provision (a marginal reading).
#ASSERT `2018 c 16 s 190 subsection 737(1) is replaced by the following` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 737(1) as replaced: convicted (or discharged under s 730) of an offence under the three Acts, subsection (1.1) does not relieve -> shall pay.
#ASSERT `s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to subsection (1.1)": where (1.1) relieves, the text says no; where its answer is not covered, so is this one.
#ASSERT `s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- not convicted or discharged, or an offence under another Act: outside the wording.
#ASSERT `s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 737(1) (not in force) the offender shall pay a victim surcharge for each offence` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2021 c. 2 s. 1(2.1) -- subsection 241.2(2.1) repealed`

#ASSERT `2021 c 2 s 1(2.1) subsection 241.2(2.1) is repealed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `2021 c 2 s 1(2.1) subsection 241.2(2.1) is repealed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2023 c. 28 s. 35 -- section 743.2 as replaced`

#ASSERT `s 743.2 (not in force) the court shall forward the item to the Correctional Service of Canada` TRUE `s 743.2 (not in force) its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 743.2 (not in force) the court shall forward the item to the Correctional Service of Canada` TRUE `s 743.2 (not in force) any relevant reports that were submitted to the court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 743.2 (not in force) the court shall forward the item to the Correctional Service of Canada` TRUE `s 743.2 (not in force) any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 743.2 (not in force) the court shall forward the item to the Correctional Service of Canada` TRUE `s 743.2 (not in force) the name and contact information for any victim who wishes to receive information under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 743.2 (not in force) the court shall forward the item to the Correctional Service of Canada` TRUE `s 743.2 (not in force) something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 743.2 (not in force) the court shall forward the item to the Correctional Service of Canada` FALSE `s 743.2 (not in force) its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The duty as a regulative rule (a DEONTIC cannot be asserted: read this result). Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 743.2 (not in force) the court must forward the reasons, reports, information and victim contact details to the Correctional Service of Canada` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 743.2 (not in force) forward to the Correctional Service of Canada its reasons and recommendation relating to the sentence or committal, any relevant reports that were submitted to the court, any other information relevant to administering the sentence or committal and the name and contact information for any victim who wishes to receive information under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` AT 1

§ `2024 c. 33 s. 2 -- subsection 679(7) as replaced`

#ASSERT `s 679(7) (not in force) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` TRUE `s 679(7) (not in force) pending the completion of the review` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(7) (not in force) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` TRUE `s 679(7) (not in force) pending a new trial or hearing directed by the Commission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(7) (not in force) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` TRUE `s 679(7) (not in force) pending the hearing and determination of a matter referred by the Commission to the court of appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 679(7) (not in force) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` TRUE `s 679(7) (not in force) at some other time` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not notified that the application is admissible: the "If" fails, the text's no within the provision (a marginal reading).
#ASSERT `s 679(7) (not in force) section 679 applies to the release or detention of the person as though the person were an appellant in an appeal described in paragraph (1)(a)` FALSE `s 679(7) (not in force) pending the completion of the review` EQUALS JUST FALSE
